<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2252" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">āmissĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				losing</i>, <i>a loss</i> (several times in Cic.,
			elsewh. rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oppidorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 17, 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dignitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 18, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnium rerum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Fam.
					4, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">foliorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 2, 2, § 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">boni, rei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Ep. 4</span></i>
			: duorum luminum, <i>of</i> (my) <i>two eyes</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Jud. 16, 28</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nullius animae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					Act. 27, 22</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">ib. Rom. 11, 15</span></i>.</div>
